---
title: Ruth's Chris Stuffed Chicken
image: https://www.easyhomemadelife.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/ruth-chris-stuffed-chicken-720x720-1.jpg
source: https://www.easyhomemadelife.com/ruth-chris-stuffed-chicken/
author: Jessica Haggard
prep time: 10 minutes
servings: 4
nutrition:
  calories: 742 kcal
  fat: 51 g
  saturated fat: 23 g
  carbohydrates: 8 g
  sugar: 3 g
  protein: 59 g
  sodium: 1082 mg
  serving size: 1 serving
cook time: 30 minutes
course: Main Dishes
time required: 40 minutes
---

Preheat oven to 450 degrees F (230 degrees C).

Mix @cream cheese{8%ounces}, @shredded cheddar cheese{1%cup}, @dry Ranch seasoning mix{1%ounce}(the garlic one is great), and @Worcestershire sauce{2%teaspoons} together in a #medium mixing bowl{}.

> You can make your own seasoning mix if you prefer. The recommended alternative is: 2 oz buttermilk powder, 2 tbsp dried parsley, 1 tbsp dried chives, 2 tsp garlic powder, 2 tsp onion powder, 1 tsp dried dill, 1/2 tsp salt, and 1/2 tsp ground black pepper. If you use this, it's only about 1/3 you need for 1 batch.

Divide the mixture into quarters. Roll each portion into a log between the palms of your hands. Aim for a log with tapered ends.

Open a pocket in each @boneless chicken breast{4%medium} by slicing lengthwise with a sharp knife, cut as deep as you can without separating the meat completely. Cut along the rounded edge.

Open and stuff one cream cheese log into each of the pockets. Use optional toothpicks to hold the breast meat in place.

Combine @salt{1/2%teaspoon}, @ground black pepper{1/4%teaspoon}, and @paprika{1/4%teaspoon} in a small bowl. Sprinkle evenly over the tops of the chicken breasts.

Arrange the stuffed chicken on a #baking sheet{} lined with parchment paper or foil.

Cook for ~{30-35%minutes} until the internal temperature reaches 165 degrees F (74 degrees C).